From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DjDeveloperr <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:01:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tipd: sn201202x: Send no LDCM command to
 a dry port

On every probe, and again after a controller reset, the driver sends an
SN201202x on a dry port an LDCM command that removes liquid-detection
mitigation, since it cannot know whether the controller is mitigating.
That command can start a new measurement, and the driver then waits up
to 5 s for it.

macOS doesn't do this. A trace of every SPMI access to the three
SN201202x controllers on a J714s (both USB-C ports and MagSafe), from
boot to the desktop, shows macOS reading the LDCM status register (0x74)
of both USB-C controllers and sending no LDCM command to any of them.
Its only commands are HChk, SSPS and, on the USB-C ports, USBw.

Do the same. Track whether this driver requested a mitigation since the
controller's last reset, and send the command that removes it only
then. A reset clears the controller's mitigation, as the driver already
assumes. The status register is still read as before, and a wet or
indeterminate port is still mitigated.

Tested on J714s (7.3.0-m5-intg6, whose tipd sources match this base),
19 boots: on every boot the driver read both USB-C controllers' LDCM
status register and sent them no LDCM command, both ports reported
contaminant "none", all three controllers bound, and the dock on the
right port came up.

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c     | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 drivers/usb/typec/tipd/tps6598x.h |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
index 1d0380ad42..3a9639e2ac 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/spmi.c
@@ -300,6 +300,19 @@ static int sn201202x_ldcm_set_mitigation(void *ctx, bool enable)
 	if (sn->ldcm_mitigation_known && sn->ldcm_mitigated == enable)
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * As macOS, which reads a dry port's status but sends it no LDCM
+	 * command: only a mitigation this driver requested since the
+	 * controller's last reset needs removing.
+	 */
+	if (!enable && !sn->ldcm_requested) {
+		sn->ldcm_mitigation_known = true;
+		sn->ldcm_mitigated = false;
+		return 0;
+	}
+	if (enable)
+		sn->ldcm_requested = true;
+
 	/*
 	 * Successful task completion is the controller's mitigation ACK.
 	 * Startup commands can take more than a second on SN201202x. Wait for
@@ -310,6 +323,8 @@ static int sn201202x_ldcm_set_mitigation(void *ctx, bool enable)
 	sn->ldcm_mitigation_known = !ret;
 	if (!ret)
 		sn->ldcm_mitigated = enable;
+	if (!ret && !enable)
+		sn->ldcm_requested = false;
 	return ret;
 }
 
@@ -465,6 +480,7 @@ static void sn201202x_ldcm_invalidate(struct tps6598x *tps)
 	tps->contaminant = TYPEC_CONTAMINANT_UNKNOWN;
 	sn->ldcm_mitigated = false;
 	sn->ldcm_mitigation_known = false;
+	sn->ldcm_requested = false;
 	sn201202x_ldcm_event(tps);
 }
 
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/tps6598x.h b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/tps6598x.h
index 68d246b739..5b975a0267 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/tps6598x.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/tps6598x.h
@@ -508,6 +508,8 @@ struct sn201202x {
 	bool ldcm_mitigated;
 	/* ldcm_mitigated matches the controller (unknown after a reset) */
 	bool ldcm_mitigation_known;
+	/* A mitigation was requested since the controller's last reset */
+	bool ldcm_requested;
 };
 
 extern const struct tipd_data *tipd_hw_variants[];
-- 
2.43.0

